# memoria.logi: where can a job run? The free memory of each machine is read by a PROGRAM (vm_stat over ssh), not typed.
#   logi spec memoria.logi                 who provides each fact, and the specification of the program
#   logi check memoria.logi --program      the conversation, on the pretend machines of `rehearse` (--world ssh:HOST for real ones)
name: memoria
about: free memory of machines

== 1. conversation
client: where can j1 run?
agent:  j1 is runnable on n2
client: where can j2 run?
agent:  j2 is runnable on n2

== 2. facts
need(J, MB)     = {J} needs {MB} MB of memory
mem_free(N:name, MB:int>=0) = {N} has {MB} MB free      [program via vm_stat]
need(j1, 48000). need(j2, 60000).

== 3. rules
runnable(J, N) = {J} is runnable on {N} | where can {J} run{N=?}
runnable(J, N) :- need(J, Need), mem_free(N, Free), Free >= Need.

== 4. meta-interpreters
-- program
rehearse n1 vm_stat: 16000
rehearse n2 vm_stat: 64000
rehearse n3 vm_stat: 32000
